Subject: [PATCH] locale: a bare tag names only the application locale

--fingerprint-locale=en-US was stored as the Accept-Language list, so
navigator.languages said ["en-US"] while the header said "en-US,en;q=0.9".
A value without a comma now names only the UI locale: it is kept as
locale.application (a child process gets the profile, not the switch) and
no list is written, so a page sees Chrome's own default list for that
locale, as a real user of it does. A comma list is still stored as given.
The voices table is keyed on the locale tag, so a bare en-US gets its
measured voices. Also closes a test body 0116 left open in compose_unittest.cc.

